 src/terminal_app.rs   |  24 +-
 src/ui.rs             | 585 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 src/ui_harness.rs     |  18 +-
 tests/terminal_app.rs |   4 +-
 tests/ui_harness.rs   | 101 ++++++++
 6 files changed, 683 insertions(+), 62 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/architecture.md b/docs/architecture.md
index 51e6cec..b386bc8 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -314,6 +314,14 @@ When an agent chat is selected in command mode, `/` focuses the chat, seeds the
 `/`, and enters insert mode so `/status`-style input submits through the same selected-agent chat
 path.
 
+In command mode, `v`, `V`, and `Ctrl-V` start character, line, and block visual selection in the
+focused pane. `h`/`j`/`k`/`l` and arrow keys move the visual cursor inside the selected pane, and `y`
+or `Y` copies the selected text to `TerminalUi`'s clipboard and queues an OSC52 terminal clipboard
+escape for the next render. Right-pane visual selection uses the same cached visible chat content and
+cursor position that `TerminalApp` and `UiHarness` pass to
+`TerminalUi::update_selectable_right_content`; while a visual selection is active, arrow keys move
+the selection instead of chat history or prompt cursor state.
+
 The terminal app maps a session to a left-pane `READY` marker when the controller exposes no loading
 state for that session. `TerminalUi` queues one terminal bell when a chat transitions into the ready
 state and renders ready rows in reverse video so they remain highlighted until the chat becomes busy
@@ -327,8 +335,9 @@ notice is observed.
 - `AgentListEntry` is the terminal left-pane representation of an agent row.
 - `TerminalLayout` computes pane geometry.
 - `TerminalUi` renders left/right panes, prompts, cursor placement, command-interface selection, and
-  terminal navigation actions. The right pane keeps the chat prompt visible while scroll offsets
-  reveal earlier transcript rows.
+  terminal navigation actions. It also owns terminal visual-selection state, clipboard text, and the
+  pending OSC52 clipboard escape emitted after a yank. The right pane keeps the chat prompt visible
+  while scroll offsets reveal earlier transcript rows.
 
 `src/ui_harness.rs::UiHarness` is the test harness for terminal behavior. It exercises the same
 `TerminalUi` frame path used by the interactive example. UI tests should drive
